3.10.text:
CHAPTER VI
PREVENTION OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 10
(1) To prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children, the Regional Government shall conduct empowerment and awareness-raising to families, parents, and the community by providing information, counseling and/or guidance.
(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness-raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall undertake efforts as follows: a. increase the quantity and quality of education both formal, non-formal and informal;
b. increase accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement, and social services; c. open employment opportunities for women;
d. build community participation and concern towards the prevention of protection of women and children from acts of violence; e. build and provide a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. build networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care about women and children; and
g. open complaint posts for the protection of women and children from acts of violence based at the sub-district level down to the village.

Article 18
(1) Regional Government forms partnerships with business entities in the protection of women and children from victims of violence.
(2) Partnership as regulated in paragraph (1) is conducted through:
a. notification of employment opportunity information for women victims of violence;
b. education and training for women victims of violence;
c. educational assistance for women and children victims of violence who have dropped out of their education;
d. fostering and increasing economic independence of women victims of violence;
e. business facilities and capital access.
(3) Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) is set forth in a joint agreement

